speechtext:
The amendment reads:
That all the words after the word "that" be struck out and the following substituted therefor:
"this bill be not now read a second time but that the subject matter thereof be referred to the committee on agriculture and colonization with instructions that they have power to recommend provision for
(1)	the regulation of interprovincial trading;
(2)	more democratic control by the producers of the proposed board or boards;
(3)	a long-range marketing programme instead of a transitional programme.
